---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import TitleLine from '../../../../components/editorial/TitleLine.astro';
import ArticleBody from '../../../../components/editorial/ArticleBody.astro';
import WorkFigure from '../../../../components/application-caching/rethink/WorkFigure.astro';
import '../../../../styles/explorables.css';
import '../../../../styles/application-caching.css';
export function getStaticPaths() {
  return process.env.APPLICATION_CACHING_DRAFT_PREVIEW === '1' ? [{params:{view:undefined}}] : [];
}
---
<Base title="Do the work once" description="A new animation study for application caching." readingPath="/">
  <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <article class="visual-essay cache-article" data-pagefind-ignore="all">
    <header class="essay-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Application caching · New visual study</p>
      <h1>Do the work once.</h1>
      <TitleLine type="Introduction" />
    </header>
    <ArticleBody>
      <p>Five shoppers ask for the same product. Their answers are identical. Watch how much work it takes to produce them.</p>
      <h2 id="same-answer">The same answer, with less work</h2>
      <WorkFigure />
      <p>A cache keeps an answer the server has already prepared. While that copy remains usable, another request can reuse it. The database stays still; the shopper gets the same card.</p>
      <section class="essay-sources" aria-labelledby="sources">
        <h2 id="sources">Sources and model notes</h2>
        <p>This illustration uses <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/patterns/cache-aside">cache-aside</a>. The invented product is north’s P7 blue mug, in English and GBP. Layout and animation timing are explanatory, not measurements. The mug drawing represents the product; the cached data contains its name and price.</p>
        <p>Reference studies: <a href="https://samwho.dev/load-balancing/">Sam Rose’s Load Balancing</a> and <a href="https://ciechanow.ski/mechanical-watch/">Bartosz Ciechanowski’s Mechanical Watch</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </ArticleBody>
  </article>
</Base>
